            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="answer-play" hidden>
          <p>
            Aim for two or more short play sessions each day. Wand toys, puzzle feeders, and chase games help
            satisfy hunting instincts and can reduce boredom-related behavior.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h2>
          <button class="question" type="button" id="question-litter" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-litter">
            How many litter boxes should I have?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="answer-litter" hidden>
          <p>
            A common rule is one litter box per cat, plus one extra. Place boxes in quiet, easy-to-reach areas
            and scoop them daily to keep the setup inviting.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h2>
          <button class="question" type="button" id="question-sleep" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-sleep">
            Why does my cat sleep so much?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="answer-sleep" hidden>
          <p>
            Cats naturally sleep for much of the day, often 12 to 16 hours. Sudden changes in sleep, appetite,
            grooming, or energy are worth discussing with a veterinarian.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h2>
          <button class="question" type="button" id="question-vet" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-vet">
            How often should my cat see a veterinarian?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="answer-vet" hidden>
          <p>
            Healthy adult cats usually benefit from an annual wellness visit. Kittens, senior cats, and cats
            with ongoing health needs may need more frequent checkups.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>General information only. Contact a veterinarian for medical advice about your cat.</p>
  </footer>

  <script>
    const faqButtons = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

    faqButtons.forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const details = document.getElementById(button.getAttribute("aria-controls"));
        const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
        details.hidden = isExpanded;
      });
    });
  </script>
